>2</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>190</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ijerph-06-00678"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruse</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirkemo</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Handeland</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wildlife as source of zoonotic infections</article-title><source>Emerg. Inf. Dis</source><year>2004</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>2067</fpage><lpage>2072</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijerph-06-00678"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>RCA</given-names></name><name><surname>Murrell</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Parasitic Zoonoses</italic> &#x02013; <italic>Emerging Issues</italic>, Thematic Issue</article-title><source>Int. J. Parasitol</source><year>2005</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1153</fpage><lpage>1332</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ijerph-06-00678"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pence</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Ueckermann</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sarcoptic manage in wildlife</article-title><source>Rev. Sci. Tech</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>398</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11974622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ijerph-06-00678"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Handasyde</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Skerratt</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Current distribution of s